From 39254b2d9f1c643e46d13c4ad1785b2275ac8f81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:38:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch 29: open the viewer and scroll back by photo id

The grid and the viewer each load their own copy of the ordered library, and the viewer was
opened with only the tapped position. After a fast scroll the two lists could disagree, so the
viewer opened a different photo, and on the way back the grid scrolled to the wrong place.

- The tapped photo's id is passed to the viewer (new optional mediaId route argument) and the
  viewer opens on the position that actually holds it
- The viewer reports the photo it ended on as id + position; the grid finds it by id
- MediaPositions.find (pure Kotlin, unit tested) does the lookup, nearest position first
- A warning is logged (tag Viewer) when the tapped position and the photo disagree
- README patch history updated
